    {
      "block_id": "page-0462-block-0002",
      "order": 2,
      "text": "The majority of people who are dependent on these classes of drugs have not obtained \nthem illegally, but are taking them as prescribed by their physician (so-called ‘iatrogenic \ndependence’).\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.0,
        62.5504150390625,
        422.7599182128906,
        98.27041625976562
      ],
      "text_sha256": "14d67c7b6c724fcbf74bd3feb653bf91adc12426137fa0da2dda04b3363838fd"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0462-block-0003",
      "order": 3,
      "text": "Long-term use of benzodiazepines is associated with a number of problems (Table \n3.27), which patients may be unaware of and only appreciate after stopping.16 Long-\nterm z-drug use is associated with similar risks.17 Gabapentinoids have been linked to \nincreased risk of suicide, unintentional overdose, road traffic accidents, and head and \nbody injuries,18 suggesting limitation of their long-term use may also be prudent.\n",
      "bbox": [
        47.9971923828125,
        98.5504150390625,
        422.82281494140625,
        158.27041625976562
      ],
      "text_sha256": "399dbf98a469a12e4f62b7bd43dc0c0a277b2889b1198043ab3b932c6d19a9e7"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0462-block-0004",
      "order": 4,
      "text": "Withdrawal symptoms\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.0,
        175.70547485351562,
